<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Savang Vatthana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–c. 1980</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Savang Vatthana was the last King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong">Sisavang Vong</a> in 1959. His reign coincided with civil war between the royal government and the communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a>, and with heavy American bombing. After the Pathet Lao took power he abdicated on 2 December 1975, and he and his family were later sent to a re-education camp, where he is believed to have died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/savang-vatthana.jpg" alt="Savang Vatthana" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Savang_Vatthana_1959.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
